# Claude handoffs (Mac Claude, on call)

Same **handover / check-in** idea as local 5090 work ([local-coder-bulk.mdc](local-coder-bulk.mdc)), but Claude can take **more context** and stronger multi-screen judgment in one call.

## Where Claude runs

- Use **Claude installed and logged in on this Mac** (Claude Code CLI or Claude Desktop).
- Do **not** use the Cursor IDE Claude agent / Bugbot-style Claude subagent for AppFly design calls.

## Package size (vs 5090)

| | Local (5090) | Claude (Mac) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Context | Condensed summaries; ≤~4–6 files per code pass | Richer pack OK: screens + API rows + privacy rules + existing patterns |
| Judgment | Mechanical only | Placement, copy, states, acceptance in one focused ask |
| Output | Code edits | Decision + copy + acceptance for a 5090 brief — not a giant patch unless asked |

Still one **concern** per call (e.g. M3 CV picker). Do not ask Claude to plan the epic or implement the feature.

## Mandatory check-in (Claude → cloud admin)

After Claude returns, **stop** before writing the 5090 brief or coding:

1. Decision clear? Open flags / method choices answered?
2. Privacy check explicit (no CV bodies in lists, no secrets, no browser job-board fetches)?
3. Acceptance criteria pasteable into a sliced 5090 brief?

Cloud admin (Grok / Cursor orchestrator) may ask one follow-up, then brief the local coder in **slices** as usual.

## Kill / escalate

- Claude auth expired / CLI unavailable → stop; ask human to re-login on Mac; do not invent M3/M6 design in cloud as a substitute without saying so.
- Vague or out-of-scope Claude reply → one re-ask with tighter output format; then escalate to human.
